    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">Given a valid Roman numeral, convert it to its integer value.<br><br>Roman numerals use seven symbols: I, V, X, L, C, D and M.<br><br>Usually, symbols are written from largest to smallest. When a smaller symbol appears before a larger one, its value is subtracted instead.<br><br>For example, IV represents 4 and IX represents 9.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\">Line 1: A string <var>S</var> representing a valid Roman numeral.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\">Line 1: The integer value represented by <var>S</var>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; |<var>S</var>| &le; 15<br><var>S</var> contains only the characters I, V, X, L, C, D and M.<br><var>S</var> represents an integer between 1 and 3999.<br><var>S</var> is a valid Roman numeral.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">I</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">1</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
